### Issue for this PR

Closes #60883

### Type of change

- [x] Bug fix
- [x] New feature

### What does this PR do?

A new session starts as a draft. The draft route mounted neither the session screen nor the side region, so the Review panel, its toggle, and every session-scoped panel were unreachable until the first message created a Session.

This mounts the shared session screen and side region on the draft route:

- The draft reserves its session id when it opens. The id is only used locally until the first message, so the Review panel has a stable session key and its stored tabs and open state survive promotion.
- Panels opt in to drafts with `Panel.drafts`. Review opts in; session-only panels keep their current behavior.
- Review reads the draft's workspace directory, including a selected worktree, so changes are available before the first message.
- Drafts stay out of `Sessions.list()`, `Sessions.current()` and `Screen.current()` unless the caller passes `{ drafts: true }`.
- Promotion copies the draft tab's side-region state to the session tab, and the reserved id keeps the stored panel state, so Review stays open after the first message.

Limitations: the draft screen is desktop-only (it has no mobile panel views yet), and Review still requires the draft's project to resolve.

### How did you verify your code works?

- Typecheck: `packages/app`, `packages/gui-plugins`, `packages/plugin`.
- Unit tests: app `src` (2584 pass) and `gui-plugins/src/review` (87 pass), including a new schema round-trip for the reserved draft id.
- E2E (Chromium): `new-session`, `review`, `side-panels` and `tabs` (144 pass before the two new cases below), plus two new cases in `new-session.spec.ts` that open Review before the first message and confirm it stays open after promotion.
- `oxlint` and `prettier` pass on the changed files. The full pre-push typecheck (33 tasks) passes.

