issues.body:
### What happened?

While editing a React component with Pi Durable, Vite cached an empty module and dropped its imported stylesheet. The file on disk was correct afterward, but reloading reused the bad transform until another file-change event invalidated it.

The underlying write race reproduces directly through `NodeExecutionEnv`, without extensions: its `writeFile()` truncates the destination before writing. The write/edit tools both use this method; coding-agent's default write/edit operations also call `fs.writeFile()` directly. Per-file mutation queues do not protect external readers such as Vite.

### Steps to reproduce

With `@earendil-works/pi-durable@1.5.2` and `@earendil-works/chord@1.5.2` installed, run this as an `.mjs` file:

```js
import { watch, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { mkdtemp, writeFile, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { NodeExecutionEnv } from '@earendil-works/pi-durable/env/node';
import { BACKGROUND_CONTEXT } from '@earendil-works/chord/context';

const dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'pi-write-race-'));
const file = join(dir, 'source.ts'), size = 1024 * 1024;
await writeFile(file, 'a'.repeat(size));
const lengths = [];
const watcher = watch(dir, (_, name) => {
  if (name === 'source.ts') lengths.push(readFileSync(file).length);
});
try {
  const env = new NodeExecutionEnv({ cwd: dir });
  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
    const result = await env.writeFile(file, (i % 2 ? 'a' : 'b').repeat(size), BACKGROUND_CONTEXT);
    if (!result.ok) throw result.error;
  }
  console.log({ empty: lengths.filter(n => n === 0).length,
    partial: lengths.filter(n => n > 0 && n < size).length, lengths: [...new Set(lengths)] });
} finally {
  watcher.close();
  await rm(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

Observed on Linux: **20 empty reads and 20 partial reads** across 20 overwrites; observed lengths were `0`, `524288`, and `1048576`. Counts will depend on filesystem scheduling.

### Expected behavior

External readers should see the complete old or new file, not an intermediate empty/partial file. Atomic per-file replacement would address this; permissions and symlink behavior need to be preserved. This does not require a multi-file transaction.

### Version

Reproduced with 1.5.2 / Node 24.22.2 / Linux 6.18.62. Upstream main still uses direct writes: [Durable](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/22fc026b872b4a7df22ffa94e8fa00b873128054/packages/durable/src/env/node.ts#L1023), [coding-agent write](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/22fc026b872b4a7df22ffa94e8fa00b873128054/packages/coding-agent/src/core/tools/write.ts#L34), [coding-agent edit](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/22fc026b872b4a7df22ffa94e8fa00b873128054/packages/coding-agent/src/core/tools/edit.ts#L89).

