## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: a node display-name selector can fail after case conversion even when its spelling is canonically equivalent to the registered name. For example, a paired node named `J̌ desk` (uppercase J plus combining caron) is found by that spelling and by its exact ID, but `ǰ desk` returns `unknown node`.

## Why This Change Was Made

Move the existing NFC normalization after the existing lowercase conversion in the shared node-name selector. Lowercasing can produce decomposed marks; composing only before conversion leaves the two selector keys different. The owner remains `src/shared/node-match.ts`, consumed by the shared node-list resolver, node CLI diagnostics and agent node helpers.

Existing-solutions preflight: JavaScript's built-in normalization and the existing shared selector are sufficient. No matching library, cache, configuration, protocol/schema, storage or plugin API is added. This follows accepted canonical matching fixes such as #195326 and #190546 at an independent owner.

## User Impact

Canonical spellings of case-converted display names select the same node. Display names and IDs remain unchanged. Exact ID/IP precedence, connected-node tie breaking, ambiguous-node errors, opt-in compact names, emoji decoration and script marks retain their existing policies. No auth, pairing, capability or invocation permission policy changes.

## Evidence

Exact-head native GREEN: **`a2ae160b342cc47e8be35bb98c5c17116553cbf7`**, **2026-11-10 14:59:27 UTC**, Linux, Node 24.22.1, OpenClaw 2026.11.2. Native RED used `96d8a35f3f4626fb818df6cb23974974c3fca6cb`; the selector and contribution contracts remain unchanged on refreshed main `d290127ec6750ac3b3504d44ab50b7cee5f92ec7`.

Recorded command: `node ../two-family-evidence/node-name-native-proof.mjs . green`. The same frozen driver runs `red` on the built baseline. It checks the build commit, creates three synthetic paired nodes through the real pairing APIs/SQLite owner, closes the seed process, starts the native built Gateway, and invokes native `nodes describe --node <name> --json`. Readback traverses real `node.list`, the shared selector and real `node.describe`; there is no fake Gateway or stubbed selector.

| Native selector | RED | GREEN |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ǰ desk` | Exit 1, unknown node | Exit 0, `fixture-node-0` |
| Original `J̌ desk` | Exit 0, same node | Exit 0, same node |
| Exact ID | Exit 0 | Exit 0 |
| `Office desk` | Exit 0 | Exit 0 |
| Decomposed `Café desk` for stored `Café desk` | Exit 0 | Exit 0 |
| Wrong-accent `j desk` | Rejected | Rejected |

Positive JSON responses preserve the original display name and show `paired: true`, `connected: false`. These are genuine persisted **offline** catalog entries, not real connected hardware. The isolated config remains unchanged.

