## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: `node_inference` cannot discover or run inference on a connected node when its display name and the query use canonically equivalent Unicode spellings, such as `Cafe\u0301 desk` and `Café desk`. With both spellings present, it can select one node instead of reporting the duplicate name.

## User Impact

Both actions accept equivalent composed/decomposed names and preserve the original display name in their results. Canonically duplicate names require an explicit node ID, just like other ambiguous names. Exact IDs, capability filtering and ordinary-name behavior remain covered.

No configuration, protocol, model identifier, dependency, stored name or migration changes; no new operator setup. This only changes comparison inside the existing Ollama tool.

## Why This Change Was Made

Normalize both name operands to NFC after lowercasing in the plugin's existing `findNode`, which owns selection for both actions. This keeps the exact-name contract; the broader SDK node resolver also accepts IPs, prefixes and punctuation-normalized names, so substituting it would expand this tool's behavior.

Existing-solutions preflight: built-in string normalization suffices. No library, new helper or SDK surface is needed. This follows the accepted Unicode name-fidelity direction in #195326 and #190546, at a separate plugin-owned selector.

