## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: the Team Reports member filter hides a member when the query and stored display name, affiliation or area use canonically equivalent Unicode spellings. For example, pasted `Café` matches only one of two members named `Café` when their strings use different accent encodings.

## Why This Change Was Made

Normalize both the query and row search text to NFC after the existing locale lowercase conversion. The shared report script serves active and quiet rows across day, week and month reports. IDs, stored data, displayed wording, ASCII handle matching and substring semantics keep their existing contracts. This does not add accent-insensitive, compatibility or fuzzy matching.

Existing-solutions preflight: JavaScript's built-in normalization is sufficient; no library, plugin, index, configuration, default or database change is needed. This follows the accepted canonical matching direction in #195326 and #190546 at a separate owner. Two production lines change; there is no separate helper or new execution path.

## User Impact

Pasted names and saved `?person=` filters find the same members regardless of composed or decomposed accents. Display text and report JSON retain their original values. Wrong accents and compatibility forms remain distinct. The report's appearance and navigation do not change.

