## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: message sends cannot resolve a directory name copied in a different Unicode normalization form, even when the channel directory has already returned the matching entry. A directory containing two equivalent spellings can also silently select only one destination.

## User Impact

Equivalent Unicode names, handles and directory IDs resolve consistently. Distinct destinations with equivalent names are reported as ambiguous so the operator can choose an explicit ID. Resolved destinations and display text keep their existing plugin-owned normalization; the directory receives the original query.

No configuration, permission, storage, schema, protocol, dependency or SDK signature changes. Accents remain significant. A raw fragment ending before an NFD combining mark no longer matches accidentally; it behaves like the corresponding NFC name already did.

## Why This Change Was Made

`resolveChannelTarget` owns the shared second filter applied after a plugin directory lookup. Normalize both lowercased comparison operands to NFC in that owner, covering ID/name/handle candidates together. Direct-ID handling, reserved-literal exactness, plugin fallback and cache keys remain on their existing paths; no helper or alternate resolver is introduced.

Existing-solutions preflight: built-in `String.prototype.normalize` is sufficient. A plugin can return correct candidates but cannot repair core discarding them. Mattermost's already-merged directory query fix #187199 is an example of an NFC-aware upstream directory; #189988 addresses the separate config-directory query predicate, not this downstream message resolver. This PR edits neither implementation. Related verified family precedent: #195326 (equivalent Unicode search).

## Evidence

Exact-head native CLI proof: `3b24a2502dae50df53b9a40e8b786b94cdea7250`; RED baseline `be82aeb77bbc08661080049650679dc602d8d197`; Linux, Node 24.22.1. Source build metadata records version `2026.11.1` and that exact head. Rechecked main `d88a384060d6d0f55920fc0092877c58d128cc3e`: owner/callers/contribution contracts unchanged.

Actual entry: `node openclaw.mjs message send --dry-run --json --channel canonical-directory-proof --target <query> --message 'Local harmless proof only'`. A loaded local channel plugin provides controlled directory entries and an outbound tripwire; the CLI bootstrap, message route, core resolver, ambiguity/reserved guards and JSON projection are real. This does not claim a live third-party directory or message delivery.

| Native CLI scenario | Baseline RED | Exact-head GREEN |
| --- | --- | --- |
| NFC name / NFD query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, `payload.to = opaque:Original-ID` |
| NFD name / NFC query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, same original destination |
| NFC handle / NFD query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, same original destination |
| NFD handle / NFC query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, same original destination |
| NFC directory ID / NFD query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, original NFC ID `Café` |
| NFD directory ID / NFC query | exit 1, `Unknown target` | exit 0, original NFD ID (`e` + U+0301) |
| Two destinations: `Café` / `Cafe` + U+0301 | exit 0, selects only first ID | exit 1, `Ambiguous target` |

