## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: rendered migration reports change literal source/target/backup paths and item metadata containing Markdown punctuation, HTML-like text or entity references. A source directory named `hermes **draft** &copy; <local>` appears as `hermes draft ©` with the final component hidden, even though `report.json` retains the actual path.

## Why This Change Was Made

Encode metadata at `writeMigrationReport`, the existing shared SDK owner of `summary.md`. Use the existing `escapeMarkdownText` helper for the title, source, optional target and backup, item ID and optional reason. JSON, item status/counters, migration execution and return types retain their contracts.

Existing-solutions preflight: the existing CommonMark text escaper solves this projection bug without a new dependency or public API. The Hermes, Claude and Codex providers already call the same writer; the fix belongs there, rather than in provider-specific wrappers. This extends the accepted literal-metadata direction of #196565 and #196004 at a separate owner.

## User Impact

Operators reading `summary.md` see the actual path and item wording. Original JSON values and secret redaction remain intact. There are no added configuration/default surfaces, protocol/schema changes, upgrade migrations, source-format changes or new operator steps.

