## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: transcript Markdown downloads and newly generated notes change meeting titles, speaker names and speech containing Markdown punctuation, HTML-like text or entity references.

## User Impact

Rendered notes retain literal wording such as `<options>`, `&copy;`, `**literal**` and backticks. Structured summaries, JSONL exports and ordinary text retain their data. Existing saved Markdown is not rewritten; regenerate notes to apply the rendering fix to an older summary.

## Why This Change Was Made

Encode transcript data at the two rendering owners using the existing CommonMark text escaper. Keep the archive's structured values unchanged. The library search also compares the encoded query against stored Markdown, preserving punctuation searches in decisions that have no matching speech or overview.

Existing-solutions preflight: the shared `escapeMarkdownText` helper already covers this contract; no new library, parser, configuration, protocol or database change is needed. This follows the accepted literal-metadata direction in #196565 and #196004, at the separate transcripts owner. Stored canonical Markdown remains intact when a download appends the full transcript.

