## What Problem This Solves

Backup commands silently trim quoted filesystem paths. `backup git init --repository '<parent>/backup '` initializes the differently named `<parent>/backup`; SQLite listing likewise reports the trimmed repository.

## Why This Change Was Made

Preserve each original nonblank path through the existing owner chain: shared backup argument resolution, snapshot directory creation via fs-safe's absolute-path API, and Git repository-root readback that removes only the terminating newline.

Existing-solutions preflight: reuse current home expansion and pinned fs-safe0.27.1 APIs; no new path library or global normalizer. Direct dependency implementation confirms absolute directory creation retains literal components and guards directory identities. Existing ancestor canonicalization, private modes/ACLs, directory pins and durable publication remain at their current owners.

This refresh merges main `4f592f12c35c631c857c206d71177f420c30ff9c` without rewriting contributor/upstream history. It resolves the shared-resolver conflict by retaining main's `ExpectedCliError` blank validation alongside this PR's literal path resolution. Backend production code and its added regressions are unchanged from the previously reviewed head `038885153418fff113651caa105b6933a44eba38`.

## User Impact

