## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: OKF imports leave valid inline links and images pointing at source filenames when destinations contain parentheses or spaces, or labels contain Markdown formatting. Import succeeds and creates the target pages, but those links remain broken.

## User Impact

User impact: imported pages link to the generated wiki pages while retaining authored labels, titles, query strings and fragments. No configuration, schema, dependency, protocol or migration changes. Reference-style links retain their prior behavior.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace the importer's regex with the Markdown parser already owned by this plugin. Rewrite only recognized inline destination spans; keep the rest of the source text intact. One source-order pass handles nested images and preserves relationship deduplication.

Existing-solutions preflight: reuse the existing `mdast-util-from-markdown` dependency and its public extension hooks, rather than add a parser or serialize whole documents. The already-merged [wiki link parsing repair](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/181380) addresses query/backlink extraction; this fixes the separate OKF import owner.

Scope: 2 files. Production +42/-59 (net -17), tests +53. No generated or lock files.

## Evidence

- Same built `wiki okf import` command and bundle before/after: **RED** `c0166c395cf81095f431808c9496cb6022ad4387` at 2026-11-15T12:48:02.179Z; **GREEN** `643e9db79ee8f13ce60dd52dcb21b89ad1b1bdb2` at 2026-11-15T13:58:21.208Z.
- Independent `marked`/JSDOM parsing of the written vault pages: before, 4 of 5 destinations still named source files; after, all 5 point to the existing generated targets. Both imports exit 0, import 4 concepts and skip 0.
- Plain-link positive control, code/external/missing-link controls and source/config byte comparisons pass on both versions. Focused tests additionally cover escaped labels/destinations, entities, multiline titles, nested images and relationship identity.
- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_RUNTIME=node node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-wiki/src/okf.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot`: **13 passed**, exit 0. The added regression failed on the unmodified branch base first (1 failed, 12 passed). Final duration 190.28s; cold compilation dominates.
- Targeted `tsgo`, typed `oxlint`, `oxfmt` and `git diff --check` pass. Final-head `node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs scripts/build-all.mts sourcePerformance` passes; this is native CLI/runtime preparation, not a full release/package check.

