**What is real:** a genuine separate OS process (`node:child_process.spawn`) generates the stream-json records and writes them to its stdout; the parent reads them over a real pipe, so frame boundaries fall where the pipe puts them. Those bytes go into the production `createCliJsonlStreamingParser`, wired with exactly the two callbacks `src/agents/cli-runner/execute-process.ts` wires (`onToolUseStart -> emitParsedToolUseStart`, `onToolResult -> emitParsedToolResult`), over the real runner consumer pair `createCliEventHandlers` + `createCliToolTracking`. The numbers above are read from the evidence projection the Gateway actually receives (`withExecutionEvidence`) and, for the `diagnostics` figures only, from the since-removed `getRetainedStateSizes()` accessor — removed in `b34efdb20df` as a test-only production seam, which is why the merged-head run below measures retained heap and exported evidence instead. The 8 MiB turn budget really is spent (at 14.0 MiB of stream), so this is the post-budget path.

**What is stubbed, and only at the outermost edge:** the run parameters come from `buildPreparedCliRunContext` (the helper the unit tests use) — no Gateway, no channel plugin, no delivery, because the finding is about what the runner *retains*, which is settled before anything is delivered. The tool-result payload the child writes is the MCP delivery fact the CLI echoes back (`details.messageDelivery.status = "settled"`), composed in the generator rather than produced by a live `message` tool call.

**Proof limits:** no Gateway process runs and no message is delivered, so this does not re-run the original production abort; it proves the retention property the review's finding is about. The retained-heap figure is corroboration, not the bound — the asserted bound is on retained evidence characters. A "before" run of the same script against the pre-fix tree was not executed in this pass (the script is written tree-agnostically so it can be: it asserts only against the public evidence projection and the heap, never a symbol the fix introduced).

