## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: opening a Template or version that ClawHub does not have (a mistyped or retired `/templates/packages/...` link, or `templates.catalog.detail` / `templates.catalog.preview` with an unknown name or version) reports "ClawHub catalog is unavailable."

## User Impact

The catalog now answers "This Template is not on ClawHub. Check the name or browse the catalog." for an unknown package and "This Template version is not on ClawHub. Choose another version." for an unknown version. A real registry failure still reads "ClawHub catalog is unavailable."

## Why This Change Was Made

`mapClawHubError` in `src/gateway/server-methods/templates.ts` is the one place the catalog methods turn errors into public messages. It kept the text only for `ClawHubSourceError`; a registry 404 arrives as `ClawHubRequestError` and fell through to the outage text. It now maps a 404 to a not-found message, using the request path (`/versions/` appears only in version and artifact requests, since package names are URL-encoded) to tell a missing version from a missing package. The same mapping existed already for plugin installs (`src/plugins/clawhub.ts:192`).

The error code stays `UNAVAILABLE` with `retryable: false`; the Control UI does not branch on catalog error codes, so it shows the new text in its existing alert. Hiding the alert's Retry button for this case is a UI change in files that #198070 is reworking, so it is not part of this PR.

