## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: previewing a file of a creator Template through its `@publisher/slug` reference (for example `@ameliomansour/openclaw-music-manager`) fails with "ClawHub artifact identity does not match the selected release." when the Template is stored under an unscoped name, although the catalog detail for the same reference works.

## User Impact

`templates.catalog.preview` now accepts the `@publisher/slug` form the docs and ClawHub show, and returns the same file as the stored name. A publisher that does not own the Template is still refused.

## Why This Change Was Made

`readClawHubTemplatePreview` (`src/templates/clawhub-source.ts:415-429`) called `requirePublicTemplatePackage` to check the publisher, then ignored the stored package it returns and passed the requested name to `readExactTemplateArtifact`. Detail and Add (`withResolvedClawHubSource`, fixed for the CLI in #198479) already continue with `pkg.name`; the preview now does the same.

The Control UI also compares the detail's `packageName` with the requested one (`ui/src/pages/agents-home/templates-catalog-client.ts:82`), so a `/templates/packages/@publisher/slug` link can still fail there. That file is reworked by #198070 and #198603, so the UI half is not part of this PR.

